+# Marginalia Books
+
+A static website for Marginalia Books, a fictional independent bookshop in Alder Bend, Oregon. It has four pages: home, books (a genre-filtered catalog), events and visit (hours, address and a contact form). It is plain HTML, CSS and vanilla JavaScript with no build step and no external requests.
+
+## View the site
+
+Serve the repository root with any static server and open the printed address. For example:
+
+```sh
+npx http-server -p 8080 -s .
+```
+
+Then open http://localhost:8080/. Opening `index.html` directly from disk also works for most pages, but the catalog is best viewed through a server.
+
+## Run the tests
+
+The tests use Node's built-in test runner and the globally installed Playwright. They start their own static server and drive headless Chromium, falling back to `/usr/bin/google-chrome` when no bundled browser is available.
+
+```sh
+NODE_PATH=$(npm root -g) node --test tests/
+```
+
+To run one file, pass its path instead, for example `tests/books.test.js`.
+
+## Layout
+
+- `index.html`, `books.html`, `events.html`, `visit.html`: the pages.
+- `css/styles.css`: the shared stylesheet.
+- `js/books.js`: the catalog data. `js/catalog.js` renders and filters it. `js/contact.js` validates the contact form.
+- `tests/`: the browser tests. `tests/index.js` loads every suite.
